DFO Forge
=========

DFO Forge is an independent, unofficial tool. It is not affiliated with or
endorsed by Bethesda Softworks or ZeniMax Media. The Elder Scrolls and
Daggerfall are trademarks of ZeniMax Media Inc.

The combat model is derived from the open-source DFO Online client:

  https://github.com/Lattymoy/daggerfall-js-source
  Snapshot: a3eb1605ea1dc391b691fe314377458a7e63e483 (2026-11-02)
  License: MIT (see the upstream LICENSE and README)

DFO Online is itself derived from Daggerfall Unity. Its combat formulas cite
and port FormulaHelper.cs, Dice100.cs, DaggerfallUnityItem.cs and DFCareer.cs
from Daggerfall Unity:

  https://github.com/Interkarma/daggerfall-unity
  License: MIT, Daggerfall Workshop

The Firmament tree and law data (vendor/firmament) and the item templates
(vendor/enchanting) come from the same MIT snapshot above. The tables in
rust/dfo-core/src/generated are derived from it by tools/rust-data.mjs, apart
from js_prototypes.rs (the JavaScript engine's own prototype names) and the
values read from this project's own src/*.js modules, some of which restate
Daggerfall Unity's formulas (attributed above).

The rules that the default game build (0.1.14631) changes relative to that
snapshot were established by reading the shipped 0.1.14631 build, which that
MIT licence does not cover.

The following upstream notices are preserved:

  Daggerfall Unity is an open-source re-implementation of The Elder Scrolls II:
  Daggerfall. It is not affiliated with Bethesda Softworks or ZeniMax Media.
  The Elder Scrolls and Daggerfall are trademarks of ZeniMax Media Inc.

DFO Forge's own MIT license text is in LICENSE. The two upstream MIT notices
below are reproduced verbatim and in full. The upstream source's own
comments and attributions are the authority for the formulas; this project
only re-expresses the parts needed for offline DPS analysis.

